{"abstract":[{"text":"A drawing whose distances match the graph’s, by stress majorization.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stressMajorizationLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"initial","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeLength","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":" = { _ in 1 }, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":" = 1e-4, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":" = 1000) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The target distance d_ij of two vertices is their shortest-path distance with ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(hops by default); between components it is 1 + L̄·√n, L̄ the mean edge length. The drawing minimizes the stress Σ_{i<j} d_ij⁻² (‖x_i − x_j‖ − d_ij)²,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which with these weights is Kamada and Kawai’s energy. Each step updates every vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order to the minimizer of a majorant of the stress in that vertex (Gansner,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Koren and North’s localized update), so the stress never increases. The run stops one step","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after a step that lowered the stress by at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" times its value (each step","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measures its starting stress on the way), or after ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" steps. A tolerance","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"below the default 10⁻⁴ can carry the run past a plateau to a lower stress.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The start is ","type":"text"},{"code":"initial","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or by default ","type":"text"},{"code":"circularLayout(radius: L̄)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Scaled by the mean edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length, the default start makes scaling every length by a power of 2 scale every step’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drawing by exactly that factor, and by any other factor up to rounding. The layout uses no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"randomness. A directed graph is drawn through ","type":"text"},{"code":"undirectedView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gansner, Koren and North, “Graph drawing by stress majorization”, Graph Drawing (GD"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2004), LNCS 3383, 2005."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Kamada and Kawai, “An algorithm for drawing general undirected graphs”, Information"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Processing Letters 31(1), 1989."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n·(n + m)) for the distances by breadth-first search (O(n·m log n) by Dijkstra when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lengths differ), then O(n²) per step. The reciprocal target distances are kept in single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"precision for the pairs i < j only, 2n² bytes (200 MB at 10⁴ vertices). ","type":"text"},{"code":"stress","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drawing are those of distances rounded to about 7 significant digits.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every edge length is positive and finite; ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance ≥ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":";","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations ≥ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; every vertex of the graph is in ","type":"text"},{"code":"initial","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", at a finite position,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when it is given.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Precondition"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/stressMajorizationLayout(initial:edgeLength:tolerance:maxIterations:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph\/stressmajorizationlayout(initial:edgelength:tolerance:maxiterations:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"stressMajorizationLayout(initial:edgeLength:tolerance:maxIterations:)","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"GraphDrawing"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P0A7DrawingE24stressMajorizationLayout7initial10edgeLength9tolerance13maxIterationsAD0C0Vy6VertexQzGANSg_Sd5Edges_5IndexQZXESdSitF","remoteSource":{"fileName":"StressMajorizationLayout.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/StressMajorizationLayout.swift#L34"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stressMajorizationLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"initial","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"e